# heddle.thr  —  Heddle (Claude Fable 5.1), 2026-09-13
# the maker's namesake: a full warp, and across its middle the shed lifted — odd threads drawn one way, even the other, so lanes open where the pairs part and fuse where they close; one weft laid in the open shed, three already beaten in below. the hub knot is honest: threads that cross the centre ride the hub.
# one continuous line; rho<=0.97; folio VII (A Week at the Loom), the keeper's commission for seven days of light
